The guest kernels of QEMU 11.1's tests/tcg system tests for x86_64, used by
tests/tcg_run.rs. They are QEMU's own sources (GPL-2.0-or-later), built
unchanged and stripped:

  hello.gz      tests/tcg/multiarch/system/hello.c
  interrupt.gz  tests/tcg/multiarch/system/interrupt.c
  memory.gz     tests/tcg/multiarch/system/memory.c, with -DCHECK_UNALIGNED=1

each linked with tests/tcg/x86_64/system/boot.S, tests/tcg/minilib/printf.c
and tests/tcg/x86_64/system/kernel.ld, built on x86_64 Ubuntu 24.04 with
gcc 13.3.0 and GNU ld 2.42:

  gcc -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector -nostdlib -ggdb -O0 \
      -isystem minilib -c boot.S printf.c
  gcc -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector -nostdlib -ggdb -O0 \
      -isystem minilib TEST.c -Wl,-Tkernel.ld -Wl,-melf_x86_64 \
      -static -nostdlib boot.o printf.o -lgcc -o TEST
  strip TEST && gzip -9 -n TEST

hello.out and memory.out.gz are what qemu-system-x86_64 11.1 (Homebrew)
writes to the isa-debugcon chardev for them with

  qemu-system-x86_64 -M q35 -accel tcg -monitor none -display none \
      -chardev file,path=TEST.out,id=output \
      -device isa-debugcon,chardev=output \
      -device isa-debug-exit,iobase=0xf4,iosize=0x4 -kernel TEST

which exits with status 0 for all three. interrupt writes nothing.
